---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import LandingHeader from "../components/LandingHeader.astro";
import LandingFooter from "../components/LandingFooter.astro";
import "../styles/landing.css";
export const prerender = true;
---

<Layout
  image="/og-image.png"
  title="Terms of use | Subabot"
  description="The scope, limitations, open-source license, and responsible use of Subabot RSS monitoring."
>
  <div class="landing-page">
    <LandingHeader />
    <main class="landing-legal" id="main">
      <span class="landing-kicker">THE PRACTICAL DETAILS</span>
      <h1>A few ground rules.</h1>
      <p class="landing-legal-lede">
        Subabot helps you monitor public feeds. These terms explain the scope of
        the tool and the responsibilities that come with using it.
      </p>
      <h2>What Subabot does</h2>
      <p>
        Subabot checks accessible public RSS and Atom feeds, matches available
        feed content against your keyword rules, and stores matching items in a
        workspace. If you connect a Slack incoming webhook, it can also send
        matching items to that destination.
      </p>
      <p>
        It is not a complete search engine. Feed coverage, publishing delays,
        network conditions, software errors, and instance configuration can
        affect results and delivery. Do not rely on it as the sole source for
        time-critical or safety-critical alerts.
      </p>
      <h2>Your workspace and connections</h2>
      <p>
        Keep your workspace access key and Slack webhook private. You are
        responsible for the feeds you add, the destinations you connect, and the
        configurations you publish. Only connect destinations that you are
        authorized to use.
      </p>
      <p>
        Use public feeds in accordance with their publishers’ terms. Do not use
        Subabot to bypass access controls, overload services, distribute spam,
        or collect information unlawfully. An instance operator may set usage
        limits or restrict activity that threatens the service or other users.
      </p>
      <h2>Source content belongs to its publisher</h2>
      <p>
        Feed items may contain material owned by third parties. A match does not
        transfer ownership or grant permission to republish that material.
        Follow the original link for full context and respect the source’s
        rights and attribution requirements.
      </p>
      <h2>Open-source software</h2>
      <p>
        The software is distributed under the{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/dorukgezici/subabot/blob/main/LICENSE">
          GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0
        </a>
        , as described in the repository’s license file. Your rights to use,
        modify, and distribute the software are governed by that license.
      </p>
      <p>
        The license includes warranty and liability terms. Read it before
        relying on or redistributing the software. These usage notes do not
        replace its terms.
      </p>
      <h2>Hosting and availability</h2>
      <p>
        This version has no paid subscription or checkout. Self-hosting may
        incur infrastructure costs. A separately operated public instance may
        have its own rules, limits, or policies. There is no uptime commitment
        for the open-source project.
      </p>
      <p>
        Keep a copy of information you need to retain. The project may change,
        and data availability depends on the server and its operator.
      </p>
      <h2>Privacy and questions</h2>
      <p>
        See <a href="/privacy">how this version handles data</a>. For questions
        about the project, inspect the{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/dorukgezici/subabot">source code</a> or
        reach the creator through{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/dorukgezici">GitHub</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="landing-legal-updated">Updated 11 October 2026.</p>
    </main>
    <LandingFooter />
  </div>
</Layout>
